-11-02-05-53-13-diskfull.json` — these are internal FLEET OPERATIONAL RECORDS (tick summaries, host names such as karahermes/bunker-mvp, incident detail), not this project's code. The remainder are the secret scanner's own detection patterns and fixtures (`.hermes/scripts/scan-git-secrets.py`, two `.bak` copies, `test_secret_scrub.py`, `gitreins-poc/sandbox/test_review_sample.py`) carrying `[REDACTED]`/fake markers, and are false positives of their own rules.\n\nNo live credential is claimed: GitHub's secret scanning on this public repo reports 0 open alerts. The defect is the published internal material itself plus the fact that the repo's own scanner arm can read green while a whole unrelated lineage is public.\n\n`master` is not historical residue — it is an ACTIVE publication channel for another project's automated jobs. Day histogram of `git log --format=%cd --date=short origin/master`: 2026-10-29..11-02 → 19/17/15/18 commits, 2026-11-03 → 5 commits. Tip and recent subjects: `qa-cron: 2026-11-03 findings (1 new, 0 deduped)` (08:42-0500, appends one line to `monitoring/.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl`), `monitoring-foreman-2026-11-03-10-55-42: recover board clobbered by e93eac07e9`, monitoring tick rows naming `bunker-mvp` and `karahermes` disk/alert detail. Each of those commits widens the public exposure, and `recover board clobbered` shows the branch is force-rewritten under no protection (CF-120).\n\nOwner decision required: retire the branch (delete `master`) or re-point it at main's history, stop the pusher, and record the residual — GitHub keeps commits reachable by SHA after a branch deletion, so a purge needs the owner's call.","acceptance_criteria":"The public ref surface and the secret-scan arm agree, at the published tip, that no unrelated lineage is published.\n\n0. Reproduce on the current tree: the row's `probe` command prints the published branch list, the count of `refs/heads/master` (expected 1 today, 0 after the fix) and the master tip's top-